# Build-time only. Read by Gradle, baked into the APK. Copy to .env and fill in.
#
# NEVER put an API token here. The phone never talks to a data provider — it talks
# to the PC, and the PC talks to the provider (ADR 0004). A value Gradle reads is a
# value compiled into the APK, and an APK is a zip file. Tokens live in
# server/config.json, which never leaves the PC.
#
# Syntax: KEY=VALUE, one per line. A line whose first non-blank character is # is a
# comment; there are no inline comments, so a value may contain #. Leading and
# trailing whitespace is stripped, and one matching pair of surrounding quotes is
# removed. Nothing sources this file in a shell — Gradle parses it (ADR 0013).

# The PC's LAN address, from the DHCP reservation made in T3.8. The app is allowed
# to reach this one host over cleartext http and nothing else. Empty or absent
# leaves the committed placeholder 192.168.1.100 in the APK, which reaches no PC.
# Changing this needs a rebuild and a reinstall: cleartext permission is a property
# of the APK, not of the server.
#
# More than one PC: a comma-separated list, PC_IP=<first-pc>,<second-pc>.
# The panel is lit while any of them answers (ADR 0016).
PC_IP=

# Private traffic (ADR 0018): the panel key and the PCs' certificates, both or
# neither. With both, data and presses go over https to each PC's TLS port with
# the key in a header, and the certificates are the only ones trusted for those
# hosts. With neither, the panel talks plain http as before, and anyone on the
# Wi-Fi can read what it reads.
#
# `python server/make_cert.py --ip <pc>` on each PC writes server/tls/<pc>.pem
# and prints a key. PANEL_KEY is the same value as panel_key in every PC's
# config.toml. PC_CERTS lists one certificate per PC, comma-separated, as paths
# relative to the repository root (the build runs in a container that mounts
# the checkout). Copy each PC's .pem here; never its .key.
#
# Every PC in PC_IP needs its certificate: a private APK talks TLS to all of
# them. A change is a rebuild and a reinstall.
PANEL_KEY=
PC_CERTS=

# Which way up the panel sits: sensorLandscape (default), landscape, or
# reverseLandscape. This is a property of the stand — which side the cable leaves
# from — and it is decided once.
#
# Leave it empty and the accelerometer decides, which is fine until the screen
# sleeps for real: the wake relaunches the activity, the phone is lying nearly
# flat, the reading is ambiguous, and the panel can come back upside down. If that
# happens, pin the one that is right for your stand. Check the current one with
# `adb shell dumpsys window | grep -o "mRotation=ROTATION_[0-9]*"`.
PANEL_ORIENTATION=

# Release signing. Absorbed from keystore.properties.
# All four empty or absent means the release build falls back to the debug key, so
# a fresh clone still builds. KEYSTORE_FILE is resolved against the Gradle root,
# which is android/ — the keystore at the repository root is ../desk-panel.keystore.
KEYSTORE_FILE=
KEYSTORE_PASSWORD=
KEY_ALIAS=
KEY_PASSWORD=
